the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a person* is authorised; scenario element.
    *a receiver* is an individual aged 16 else over; scenario element.
    *a receiver* is a body; scenario element.
    *an effect* is detrimental; scenario element.
    *an effect* is of a persistent else continuing nature; scenario element.
    *an effect* affects the quality of life of those in the locality; scenario element.
    the conduct for *a receiver* is *a conduct*; scenario element.
    the effect for *a conduct* is *an effect*; scenario element.
    *a conduct* is unreasonable; scenario element.
    *a person* may issue a community protection notice for *a receiver*.
    the conduct in may issue a community protection notice for *a receiver* variant one is *a conduct*.
    the effect in may issue a community protection notice for *a receiver* variant two is *an effect*.

the knowledge base anti_social includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/anti-social.l4".

section anti social is:

the conduct in may issue a community protection notice for a receiver variant one is a conduct if
    the conduct for the receiver is the conduct.

the effect in may issue a community protection notice for a receiver variant two is an effect if
    the conduct in may issue a community protection notice for the receiver variant one is a conduct
    and the effect for the conduct is the effect.

a person may issue a community protection notice for a receiver if
    the person is authorised
    and the receiver is an individual aged 16 else over
        or the receiver is a body
    and the effect in may issue a community protection notice for the receiver variant two is an effect
    and the effect is detrimental
    and the effect in may issue a community protection notice for the receiver variant two is a second effect
    and the second effect is of a persistent else continuing nature
    and the effect in may issue a community protection notice for the receiver variant two is a third effect
    and the third effect affects the quality of life of those in the locality
    and the conduct in may issue a community protection notice for the receiver variant one is a conduct
    and the conduct is unreasonable.

